6-08-06T17:59:15Z","updated_at":"2026-08-11T16:46:23Z","closed_at":"2026-08-11T16:46:23Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.7.stable.official [5b4e0cb0f]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.stable - Linux Mint 22.3 (Zena) on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - integrated AMD Radeon 780M Graphics (RADV PHOENIX) - AMD Ryzen 7 PRO 8840HS w/ Radeon 780M Graphics (16 threads) - 27.05 GiB memory - PulseAudio (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nAfter saving a resource from the inspector, all the fields collapse making it annoying to edit, create, and save resources in this workflow. I expect the inspector to remain as I had it when I saved the resource.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. In the sample project, open TestResource.tres in the inspector by double clicking it in the FileSystem tab.\n2. There is an array of two sub-resources here, each with an array of sub-sub-resources. Open out either of the sub-resources.\n3. In one of the unassigned sub-sub-resource slots, create a new sub-sub-resource.\n4. Right click your new sub-sub-resource, and click save.\n5. Save the resource with a unique filename.\n6. Note that the inspector has collapsed, requiring you to open out the tree again to find the sub-sub-resources you were working with.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[inspector-resource-save-bug-report.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/30799346/inspector-resource-save-bug-report.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repi